{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimedEvent"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DarknessTimeAndDeath","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Timer names are bare strings wherever they are unambiguous. Two owners"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(the game and a bundle, or two bundles) may both declare one name: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bootstrap moves each bundle-owned declaration into its namespace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"Clock.roam\""},{"type":"text","text":") while the game’s own stays bare, and a body running for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its owner resolves the bare literal it declared against that owner first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startFuse(_:after:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and friends). A host game addresses a bundle’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collided timer by the qualified name."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Timers tick once per typed command, at the very end of the turn (after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the world’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"type":"text","text":"\/each-turn rules): fuses first, then daemons, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"group in name order. They tick on refused turns (world time passes) but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not on parse errors, meta commands, or once the game has ended. A timer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"started by a rule ticks at the end of that same turn — so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fuse(after: 1)"},{"type":"text","text":" started by a rule fires as that very turn ends. A timer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"started from "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"inside a fuse or daemon body"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a turn behind that: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tick reads both schedules once before it runs any body, so the new timer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first ticks at the end of the next turn."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimedEvent"}],"title":"TimedEvent","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"externalID":"s:6Gnusto10TimedEventV","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimedEvent"}],"role":"symbol"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A named timed event, declared in a game or bundle ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block: a fuse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(fires once, N turns after it is started) or a daemon (runs at the end of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every turn while active). The body is registered at bootstrap and never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"serialized; only the schedule — name → turns remaining, or the active","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flag — lives in ","type":"text"},{"code":"WorldState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it saves and restores like any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state and a restore re-binds it to the declared body by name.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DarknessTimeAndDeath","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuse(_:after:autostart:perform:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/daemon(_:autostart:perform:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startFuse(_:after:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopFuse(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuseRemaining(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startDaemon(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopDaemon(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/isDaemonActive(_:)"],"title":"Time, Light, and Death","anchor":"Time-Light-and-Death"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/timedevent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"title":"Gnusto","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/fuse(_:after:autostart:perform:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Declares a fuse: ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs once, ","type":"text"},{"code":"turns","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" turns after the fuse is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"started — by ","type":"text"},{"code":"startFuse(_:after:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a rule, or from turn one with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"autostart","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Starting a running fuse resets its count.","type":"t